From c9d83fecaaf9939ae50924fb022ff760d452acb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 06:24:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] perf(render): skip culling task lists for full
 occlusion queues

Rails, vehicles and lifts built one culling lambda per object every frame and
offered the batch to a two-slot ArrayBlockingQueue, which silently drops the
offer when full. Check the queue's remaining capacity first and skip building
the list when the offer could not be accepted. The worker may still poll
between the check and the offer; that frame then behaves as if it had polled
just after the offer, a timing the original already allowed. Shadow passes and
MSD's rail queue are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TD7PJ5R7t7hM3ymeeqXP4H
